Xray-core: closing a WireGuard outbound no longer panics a sender

The WireGuard outbound without a kernel TUN (noKernelTun, or any phone,
which has no CAP_NET_ADMIN) runs a gVisor stack on netTun. The stack hands
each packet it sends to netTun.WriteNotify, on the sender's own goroutine,
and WriteNotify waits on the unbuffered incomingPacket channel until
wireguard-go's TUN reader takes it. netTun.Close closed that channel. A
sender still waiting there when the outbound closed under traffic panicked
with "send on closed channel" (netstack.go:169) on a goroutine of the stack
or of wireguard-go, where nothing recovers, and the process ended. On
2026-10-19 that ended the app's main process during a WireGuard lab test on
the emulator: wireguard-go's receive routine handed in data for a
connection the check had closed, and the stack's reset waited in
WriteNotify. A TCP sender waiting there also holds its endpoint's lock,
which stack.Close takes, so with no reader Close could wait for ever.

incomingPacket is no longer closed. Close closes a new channel, closed,
first and once. WriteNotify drops its packet when it sees it, and Read
returns os.ErrClosed as before, so wireguard-go's reader stops and
device.Close returns. Upstream Xray-core later rewrote netTun with the same
closed channel in 8703fdb10147 (#7156, 2026-10-15), which also replaced
gVisor with Xray-core's own TCP/IP stack. That commit is in v26.10.17
(92ccc939aaf4) and later, and needs Go 1.27, so this core cannot take it.

Handler.init also set the bind's listen and resolve functions after
device.NewDevice, whose TUN event reader opens the bind at once on its own
goroutine (bind.Open calls listenFunc). They are now set before it.

Base:    github.com/xtls/xray-core v1.260327.1-0.20260728075948-5ca6f4b7d4dc
         (v26.7.28). Touches no file the other patches touch.
Licence: netstack.go: MIT, the licence it carries (its SPDX line).
         client.go and the new netstack_close_test.go: MPL-2.0, the same
         as Xray-core. The test was written for Fortiva.

  proxy/wireguard/netstack.go             closed, closeOnce; Read,
                                          WriteNotify, Close
  proxy/wireguard/netstack_close_test.go  a sender waiting in WriteNotify
                                          when the device closes
  proxy/wireguard/client.go               the bind's functions are set
                                          before NewDevice

Apply with: patch -p1 < xray-wireguard-close.patch   (stage-xray.sh does this)

